# Line endings, pinned — added when this repo started being worked on from
# Windows as well as Linux.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout for everything it considers text. For
# most files here that is harmless. For three kinds of file it is not:
#
#   *.sh          a CRLF shebang line makes the kernel look for an
#                 interpreter literally named "bash\r", and the script
#                 dies with a "bad interpreter" error that names an
#                 invisible character. Equally, `dev.sh` and friends are
#                 run through Git Bash and WSL on this machine and on a
#                 real Linux box; they must be byte-identical in both.
#   Dockerfile    same problem one layer down — the image is built from
#                 this tree and runs on Linux regardless of what built it.
#   *.pem, images, the model
#                 binary. CRLF translation corrupts them outright.
#
# `* text=auto` keeps the repository itself normalised to LF (what is
# stored is LF no matter who commits), and the explicit `eol=lf` entries
# below override the checkout half for the files that cannot survive it.
* text=auto

# Executed as scripts on Linux, and by Git Bash on Windows. LF always.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerignore  text eol=lf

# Windows-only, and PowerShell is happy either way — but keeping it CRLF
# matches what every Windows editor will write back anyway, so the file
# does not show up as modified after being opened.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Source. LF everywhere: these are read by tools (pytest, vitest, tsc,
# Vite) that do not care, and by two operating systems that do.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.tsx           text eol=lf
*.mts           text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.example       text eol=lf

# Binary — never translated, never diffed as text.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.docx          binary
*.xlsx          binary
*.onnx          binary
*.pem           binary
*.pt            binary
